## Vault Path
`[absolute path to vault folder]`

## Structure
| Folder | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `1 Projects/` | Active work, scored 1-5 → Priority (4-5) / Important (2-3) / Idea Dump (1) |
| `2 Areas/` | Ongoing responsibilities: Role & Strategy, Team, Stakeholders, Hiring |
| `3 Reference/Raw/` | Unprocessed drops (web clips, Drive links, notes) |
| `3 Reference/Wiki/` | Synthesized domain knowledge — cumulative, never overwritten. Organized into topic subfolders. |
| `4 Archives/` | Completed projects |
| `5 People/[Name]/` | One folder per person — no VIP/Team split. Contains: `[Name].md` (WIKI) + `1-on-1/` subfolder |
| `5 People/[Name]/[Name].md` | Person WIKI — cumulative knowledge, relationship intelligence, all 1:1 notes, personality, managing hints |
| `5 People/[Name]/1-on-1/` | All 1:1 prep docs + Granola meeting summaries for that person |
| `5 People/People Intelligence Map.md` | Master relationship map — all key people, influence scores, managing edges, watch-outs |
| `6 Reviews/Daily/` | Cumulative daily digest (new + open carry-forwards only) — index newest first |
| `6 Reviews/Daily/Jira/` | Daily Jira/Linear updates — sprint status + stakeholder asks (newest first) |
| `6 Reviews/Team/` | Team sprint snapshot — separate daily file |
| `6 Reviews/Weekly/` | Weekly retro + Leadership OS scores |
| `7 Metrics & KPIs/` | WBR, MBR, QBR, Anomalies, Metric Definitions (SSOT) |
| `8 [FIRSTNAME]'S BRAIN/` | Schema, About [First Name], Memory, Agents, Command Center |
| `Granola/` | Daily meeting digests — processed recaps per day, indexed newest-first |
| `Granola/Transcripts/` | Raw Granola output — never modify |

## Core Rules
1. Read `8 [FIRSTNAME]'S BRAIN/About [First Name].md` before acting — every session
2. Daily notes are cumulative — carry forward unchecked items, never repeat resolved
3. People pages = single source of truth — update after every interaction
4. All people are one level — no VIP/Team folders. Surface by influence score: highest →[Name] score first
5. Raw → Wiki only on request via `wikify` — wiki pages accumulate, never overwrite. Place every new wiki page in the correct category subfolder. Suggested categories:
   - `Revenue & Monetization/` — revenue, billing, pricing, ad models
   - `Data & Metrics/` — data models, event schemas, session metrics, data warehouse tables
   - `Platform & Product/` — platform features, product areas, taxonomy
   - `Marketing & Growth/` — traffic attribution, marketing spend, growth analytics
   - `Strategy & Roadmap/` — OKRs, roadmaps, org structure, quarterly planning
   - `Leadership & Operations/` — leadership frameworks, hiring, onboarding, personal effectiveness
6. Commands have no prefix — just type the name — see `8 [FIRSTNAME]'S BRAIN/Command Center.md`
7. Coach [First Name] to say NO when overcommitting — use `3 Reference/Wiki/Say No Playbook.md`
8. Flag hedging language in leadership emails
9. [Tool] board: [Board URL]
10. **After any structural change** (new command, new folder, new workflow) — update `8 [FIRSTNAME]'S BRAIN/Command Center.md`, `8 [FIRSTNAME]'S BRAIN/Memory.md`, and the relevant `HOW TO BUILD ME/` doc. Keep them in sync always.
30. **After updating CLAUDE.md or any `8 [FIRSTNAME]'S BRAIN/HOW TO BUILD ME/` doc** — sync changes to the GitHub second-brain template (replace personal details with placeholders), commit, and push. This keeps the public template current with vault evolution.

## Granola Rules (read from vault — never via MCP)
11. **All Granola transcripts live in** `Granola/Transcripts/` — read them directly as files. Never rely solely on the MCP for Granola data; the vault is always the source of truth.
12. **Every transcript must have a date header** — format: `> 📅 **YYYY-MM-DD**` immediately after the `# Transcript for:` heading. Add on first read if missing.
13. **Index Granola 1:1s → person's WIKI + 1-on-1 folder** — after any 1:1 transcript is read:
    - Identify the person → find their folder at `5 People/[Name]/`
    - Append `### YYYY-MM-DD — [Meeting Title]` to `## 1:1 Notes` in `[Name].md` (WIKI): topics, key signals, action items (theirs + mine), relationship delta (did trust go up/down?)
    - Update `## Interactions` log (newest first)
    - Update `## Open Action Items`
    - Create or append to `5 People/[Name]/1-on-1/YYYY-MM-DD.md` — full Granola summary: TLDR, decisions, actions, key observations
    - Extract any personality/RI signals → update `## Relationship Intelligence` section in WIKI (append new observations, update influence score if something shifted)
    - If influence score changed or a new managing insight emerged → update `5 People/People Intelligence Map.md` Changelog
14. **Team standups → `5 People/[Team Name] Standups.md`** — append each standup as a new dated section (newest first). Never overwrite. Include: key discussions, decisions, action items table.
15. **Daily Granola recap in daily note** — append a `## Granola — [Date]` section to today's daily note for every meeting processed:
    ```
    ## Granola — YYYY-MM-DD
    ### [Meeting Title]
    - **TLDR:** ...
    - **Actions (mine):** ...
    - **Actions (theirs):** ...
    - **RI signal:** [any personality/behavior observation worth capturing]
    ```
16. **Mark transcripts as indexed** — after completing rules 12–15, append filename to `~/.claude/granola_indexed.txt`. Command: `echo "filename.md" >> ~/.claude/granola_indexed.txt`

## People & 1:1 Prep System
20. **Person folders** — every person gets `5 People/[Person Name]/`. No VIP/Team subfolders — flat structure.
21. **Person WIKI (`[Name].md`)** — cumulative knowledge base inside the person's folder. Sections: Relationship Intelligence (personality, influence scores, managing edge, watch-outs), About, 1:1 Cadence, 1:1 Notes (newest first), Key Intelligence, Interactions (newest first), Open Action Items. Never overwrite — always append.
22. **`1on1` command** — when [First Name] says "prepare for 1:1 with [Person]": read their WIKI (especially Relationship Intelligence section) + all files in their `1-on-1/` subfolder + Jira tickets + Slack. Generate `YYYY-MM-DD.md` in `5 People/[Name]/1-on-1/`. After meeting: update WIKI, append Granola summary to `1-on-1/YYYY-MM-DD.md`, update People Intelligence Map influence score if something shifted.
23. **1:1 file naming:** `YYYY-MM-DD.md` always inside `5 People/[Name]/1-on-1/`.
24. **People Intelligence Map** — after any meaningful relationship shift (trust up/down, influence score change, new personality signal), update `5 People/People Intelligence Map.md`. Keep the master table and Changelog current.

## Jira / Linear Daily Update Rules
17. **`jira-update` command** — pull sprint status + stakeholder channel for new asks. Write to `6 Reviews/Daily/Jira/YYYY-MM-DD.md`. Sections: New Asks (needs ticket), Sprint Status by person, Sprint Health Summary, Tickets to Create table. Append a one-line summary to `6 Reviews/Daily/Jira/_Index.md` (newest first, manually maintained above the dataview block).
18. **Daily Jira `_Index.md` ordering** — always newest first. Manually prepend the new entry line; never append to the bottom.
19. **Daily `_Index.md` ordering** — same rule: manually prepend each new day's entry above the previous one in `6 Reviews/Daily/_Index.md`. The dataview block handles Obsidian rendering; the manual list handles raw markdown navigation.

## Relationship Intelligence Rules
25. **Every person page has a `## Relationship Intelligence` section** — cumulative, never overwritten. Subsections: Personality Profile, Strengths, Weaknesses & Blind Spots, What They Expect from [First Name], How to Influence & Work With Them, Influence Scores ([First Name]→them / them→[First Name], scored /5), Impact Record.
26. **Extract RI signals from every Granola transcript and interaction** — after reading any 1:1 transcript or standup, look for: personality signals (how they communicate, react, decide), new strengths/weaknesses observed, shifts in trust or mood, moments of influence ([First Name]'s words or actions that changed something). Append findings to the person's RI section. Never overwrite — always append with date.
27. **1:1 prep always surfaces RI hints** — every `1on1` prep brief must include a **Relationship Intelligence Brief** block: personality reminder, 1-2 influence tactics for this specific meeting, current influence score, and 1 thing to do to move the score up.
28. **Influence score updates** — after any interaction where [First Name] visibly changed someone's thinking, decision, or behavior, update their Influence Score and log it in Impact Record with date + what happened.
29. **Charismatic, not people-pleasing** — all relationship coaching must default to confident, direct, strategic influence. Never suggest [First Name] accommodate, defer, or soften to avoid conflict. Suggest reframing, timing, and charismatic persuasion instead.

## Friday Closeday Rule
24b. **`closeday` on Friday = weekly close** — when run on a Friday, in addition to standard EOD steps, always:
    - Create `6 Reviews/Weekly/YYYY-Wxx.md` (ISO week number) with: week recap (✅ shipped, ⚠️ carried over, 💡 observations), next week priorities table built from the user's closeday input, Leadership OS score template, NO tracker
    - Prepend a one-line entry to `6 Reviews/Weekly/_Index.md` (newest first, above the dataview block)
    - Run `lint` after closeday completes
    - End the session with a goodbye

## Relationship Graph Rules
31. **`graph` command** — regenerates `5 People/Relationship Graph.html` from `5 People/People Intelligence Map.md` and all person WIKI files. Output is a standalone interactive HTML file using vis.js from CDN (no Python, no installs). Opens in browser automatically after generation.
32. **Auto-suggest `graph` after any influence score change** — whenever an influence score is updated in People Intelligence Map or any `[Name].md` WIKI, end the update with: "Influence score changed — run `graph` to update your relationship visualization."
33. **Graph encodes:** node size = →[First Name] score, indigo arrows = [First Name]→ person influence, slate arrows = person→ [First Name] influence, gold dashed = org hierarchy. Hover any node for personality, managing edge, watch-out.
34. **Data tools** — connect via skill commands (e.g. `/snowflake` for Snowflake SSO). Store connection details in `8 [FIRSTNAME]'S BRAIN/About [First Name].md` under Tech Stack.

## Automation Hook
A `SessionStart` hook runs `~/.claude/granola-check.py` at the start of every session. It compares `Granola/Transcripts/*.md` against `~/.claude/granola_indexed.txt` and displays a banner if unindexed transcripts are found. When you see this banner, run `granola` to process them.

